### Ledger API — live request collection
#
# Open this file in Kiro/VS Code (install the "REST Client" extension) or IntelliJ,
# and a "Send Request" link appears above each ### block. Click it and the response
# opens in a side panel.
#
# Why this file is in the repo: it is version-controlled documentation that actually
# runs. A new developer clones, starts the app, and clicks through the whole API
# without installing Postman or writing a single curl command.
#
# Before running: docker compose up -d --wait  &&  ./mvnw spring-boot:run

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Health check
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### Balance of an account
# Replace the UUID with a real one from your database:
#   docker exec ledger-postgres psql -U ledger -d ledger -c "select id, account_type from accounts;"
GET {{host}}/accounts/aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/balance

### Transfer money  (expect 201)
POST {{host}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "toAccountId": "bbbbbbbb-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
  "amountMinor": 50000,
  "description": "A pays B Rs 500"
}

### Same request again — idempotent replay (expect the SAME transactionId, no second debit)
POST {{host}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "toAccountId": "bbbbbbbb-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
  "amountMinor": 50000,
  "description": "A pays B Rs 500"
}

### Unknown account  (expect 404, error = account_not_found)
GET {{host}}/accounts/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999/balance

### Insufficient funds  (expect 400, error = transfer_rejected)
POST {{host}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-too-big

{
  "fromAccountId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "toAccountId": "bbbbbbbb-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
  "amountMinor": 99999900,
  "description": "more than the balance"
}

### Validation failure  (expect 400 with fields.amountMinor)
POST {{host}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-negative

{
  "fromAccountId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "toAccountId": "bbbbbbbb-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
  "amountMinor": -500,
  "description": "negative"
}

### Transfer to the same account  (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-self

{
  "fromAccountId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "toAccountId": "aaaaaaaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "amountMinor": 100,
  "description": "self transfer"
}
